{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-1","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · explainer-video：Turn a directory of structured coursework notes, or a codebase's major code flows,\ninto a narrated, animated explainer-video series.\n\nA skill for AI coding agents — Claude Code, Codex, DeepSeek Harness and\nAntigravity. Point it at a folder of course notes: it plans the series, writes\nthe narration, synthesizes the audio, authors the visuals, then renders and\nassembles finished MP4s with YouTube-ready chapters and captions.","source":"extracted","section":"explainer-video"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-2","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · explainer-video：Its planner does not merely invent titles — it **proves completeness**: every\ncontent-bearing section is assigned to a video or classified as navigation\n(`0 orphaned`) before any expensive stage runs.","source":"extracted","section":"explainer-video"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-3","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · The pipeline：Stage 0 (`/inputs`) collects the two things only you can decide — the source\nnotes directory, and where the finished videos land — plus, optionally, the playlist\nname a series is published under (it is never guessed; a series left blank is asked about at 6b).","source":"extracted","section":"The pipeline"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-4","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · The pipeline：| # | stage | what it does | cost |\n|---|-------|--------------|------|\n| 1 | `/plan` | decompose the notes, prove coverage | free, local |\n| 2 | `/enrich` | retitle and curate (skip / merge) | free, agent |\n| 3 | `/script` | write the narration segments | free, agent |\n| 4 | `/audio` | TTS → a measured timeline | **network — spends the Gemini key** |\n| 5 | `/scene` | author the visuals (`diagram` / `code` / `svg`) | free, agent |\n| 6 | `/publish` | YouTube chapters + captions | free — no TTS, no Chromium |\n| 6b | `/thumbnail` | a 1280x720 `thumbnail.png`: one hook over a still from the video's own scenes, plus a `<playlist>-Part X, <title>` label for a series | free — one Chromium screenshot |\n| 7 | `/render` | frames → H.264 MP4 | local CPU |\n| 8 | `/assemble` | per-segment parts → the finished cut | local CPU |","source":"extracted","section":"The pipeline"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-5","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · The pipeline：Stages 1–2 run once for the whole directory; stages 3–8 run once per video. One\nvideo end to end is a valid stopping point — a pilot, or a single-target run.","source":"extracted","section":"The pipeline"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-6","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Install：> **Renamed.** This plugin was published as `explainer-video-from-coursework`; it is now\n> `explainer-video`. The skills inside are unchanged — `/explainer-video-from-coursework` and\n> `/explainer-video-from-codebase` keep their names. If you installed the old name, uninstall it\n> and install the new one: `claude plugin uninstall explainer-video-from-coursework@akshaydev17`\n> then `claude plugin marketplace update akshaydev17` and the install line below (Codex and\n> DeepSeek Harness: remove the old name the same way, then add `explainer-video`). Antigravity\n> installs from git and needs nothing. The old npm package stays published but receives no new\n> releases.","source":"extracted","section":"Install"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-7","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Install：**Claude Code**\n\n```sh\nclaude plugin marketplace add akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video\nclaude plugin install explainer-video@akshaydev17\n```\n\n**Codex**\n\n```sh\ncodex plugin marketplace add akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video\ncodex plugin add explainer-video@akshaydev17\n```\n\n**DeepSeek Harness**\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add explainer-video\n```\n\n**Antigravity**\n\n```sh\nagy plugin install https://github.com/akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video\n```","source":"extracted","section":"Install"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-8","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Install：All four commands install the **same** npm package — one package, three manifest surfaces,\none copy of all seventeen skills: the eleven video skills, `coursework-author`, the companion\nskill for writing the coursework these videos come from, and the five code-flow skills:\n`explainer-video-from-codebase`, which makes explainer videos of a codebase's major code flows\n(Python, TypeScript / JavaScript, Go, C, C++, or a mix), and its four stage skills. It mines the\nrepo, ranks candidate flows, optionally traces the test suite in a sandbox, has you approve the\nflow list, plans the videos, then runs the same per-video stages with verified code panels and\ngenerated flow diagrams. How each platform reads it, and how\nto publish, is in\n[`DISTRIBUTION.md`](./DISTRIBUTION.md).","source":"extracted","section":"Install"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-9","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Prerequisites：- **Node ≥ 22** — `render.mjs` relies on the built-in global `WebSocket`.\n- **`ffmpeg` + `ffprobe`** — H.264 encoding, muxing, and duration measurement.\n- **Headless Chromium** — `npx playwright install --with-deps --only-shell`.\n- **A Gemini API key** — for TTS. It lives in the **OS secret store** (macOS\n  Keychain · Linux `secret-tool` · Windows Credential Manager) under the service\n  name `gemini-tts` — never in env, never in a plaintext file. A free key:\n  <https://aistudio.google.com/apikey>.","source":"extracted","section":"Prerequisites"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-10","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Prerequisites：The tools **fail loud** on a missing prerequisite rather than quietly producing a\nbroken video. Per-OS commands and citations:\n[`SETUP.md`](./skills/explainer-video-from-coursework/SETUP.md).","source":"extracted","section":"Prerequisites"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-11","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Use it：Invoke the skill with the notes directory:\n\n```\n/explainer-video-from-coursework path/to/your/notes/\n```\n\nYou get one `.mp4` per video, plus `title.txt`, `description.md` (blurb and a\npaste-ready chapter block), `captions.srt` and a `thumbnail.png`, copied to the\ndestination you chose — by default `videos/` beside the source. Scratch stays in a gitignored\n`out/<name>/<NN>/`.\n\nFor a codebase, invoke the code-flow skill with the repo root instead:","source":"extracted","section":"Use it"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-12","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Use it：```\n/explainer-video-from-codebase path/to/your/repo/\n```\n\nIt shows you the ranked candidate flows and its proposed series, and plans no video until you\napprove the flow list. Its scratch root sits outside the repo.\n\nRun every command from the **project** (where `out/` lives), not from the skill's\ninstall folder. The tools self-locate their own `tools/`, `src/` and `scenes/`,\nso only the work and scratch paths depend on the current directory.","source":"extracted","section":"Use it"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-13","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Repository layout：```\nplugin.json                              Agent Plugins manifest (Codex, Antigravity)\n.claude-plugin/                          plugin.json + marketplace.json (Claude Code)\n.agents/plugins/                         marketplace.json (Codex)\ncordis.patch.yml + lib/index.js          DSH bundle plugin (serves this package's skills/)","source":"extracted","section":"Repository layout"}
{"unit_id":"akshayDev17__ai-explainer-video#readme-14","repo":"akshayDev17/ai-explainer-video","commit":"b4fcffa8d542c85ca4169ca345b7999b00fe0f02","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"explainer-video README · Docs：| file | what it covers |\n|------|----------------|\n| [`SKILL.md`](./skills/explainer-video-from-coursework/SKILL.md) | the contract of record — the agent's entry point |\n| [`SKILL.md`](./skills/explainer-video-from-codebase/SKILL.md) (codebase) | the code-flow pipeline's contract of record |\n| [`FLOWS.md`](./skills/explainer-video-from-codebase/FLOWS.md) | every code-flow artifact's fields, from the code map to the code panels |\n| [`SETUP.md`](./skills/explainer-video-from-coursework/SETUP.md) | cited, per-OS machine prerequisites |\n| [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](./skills/explainer-video-from-coursework/ARCHITECTURE.md) | how the pieces fit together |\n| [`PIPELINE.md`](./skills/explainer-video-from-coursework/PIPELINE.md) | the stage-by-stage pipeline |\n| [`ROADMAP.md`](./skills/explainer-video-from-coursework/ROADMAP.md) | design record and open work |\n| [`DISTRIBUTION.md`](./DISTRIBUTION.md) | publishing, and installing on each platform |\n| [`RELEASING.md`](./RELEASING.md) | how a release works — a dispatch, not a merge |","source":"extracted","section":"Docs"}
